#!/usr/bin/env llmsh
---
name: deploy
description: Deploy a project to a remote server
model: claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929
provider: anthropic
tools:
  - bash
  - read_file
  - list_files
  - env
args:
  - name: target
    description: Deployment target (e.g., staging, production)
    required: true
  - name: branch
    description: Git branch to deploy
    default: main
permissions:
  - read
  - execute
max_turns: 15
temperature: 0.0
---

You are a deployment assistant. Deploy the current project to the specified target.

1. First, check the current git status and ensure the working directory is clean
2. Verify you're on the correct branch ({{.Args.branch}})
3. Run any build steps if a Makefile, package.json, or similar exists
4. Report what would be deployed

Target environment: {{.Args.target}}
Branch: {{.Args.branch}}
